abstract: >-
  Reading notes for ENG 101 Programming for Engineers at Nazarbayev
  University. A 216-page book that introduces the programming languages an
  engineer meets (Python, Fortran, C, C++, C#, Java, JavaScript, MATLAB, the
  Wolfram Language, R, Julia and others), with every complete example program
  provided as a file together with its real output. The same small
  engineering problem, a falling body with air drag solved by the Euler
  method, is programmed in every language, and three numerical tasks are
  compared side by side in thirteen languages.
